010 census its population was 495. Its elevation is about 870 meters. Nearby places include Cabeça Fundão to the north, Figueira Pavão to the east, Fonte Aleixo to the south and Monte Largo to the west. Its climate is cooler than the low-lying areas of the island. The average temperature is . Average rainfall is 366 millimeters, the highest is 149 mm in September and the lowest is\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0254-625ff1f99c77:d01\", \"text\": \"11,966 +2,778 2000 16,895 14,311 +2,584 2001 18,955 13,153 +5,802 2002 18,112 12,891 +5,221 2003 17,838 12,083 +5,755 2004 20,333 13,656 +6,677 2005 21,355 12,369 +8,986 2006 22,451 12,107 +10,344 2007 26,029 12,443 +13,586 2008 29,114 13,657 +15,457 2009 26,699 12,151 +14,548 2010 25,636 11,905 +13,731 2011 29,481 12,660 +16,821 2012 31,278 13,845 +17,433 2013 31,941 13,893 +18,048 2014 31,507 15,486 +16,021 2015 28,746 16,305 +12,441 2016 34,905 18,082 +16,823 2017 31,797 16,973 +14,824 2018 31,106 19,141 +11,965 2019 32,758 17,263 +15,495 2020 32,898 15,084 +17,814 2021 36,364 13,459 +22,905 2022 49,998 15,635 +34,363 2023 73,236 15,322 +57,914 Statistics of\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0254-625ff1f99c77:d02\", \"text\": \"3,564 1.1 % 1,822 1,743 51.1 % 48.9 % 1.05 < 5 18,827 5.7 % 9,624 9,203 51.1 % 48.9 % 1.05 < 15 60,467 18.2 % 30,989 29,578 51.2 % 48.8 % 1.05 15-24 43,089 13.0 % 21,996 21,092 51.0 % 49.0 % 1.04 25-34 45,495 13.7 % 23,053 22,442 50.7 % 49.3 % 1.03 35-44 43,404 13.1 % 21,858 21,546 50.4 % 49.6 % 1.01 45-54 40,688 12.3 % 20,312 20,376 49.9 % 50.1 % 0.99 55-64 42,803 12.9 % 20,963 21,840 49.0 % 51.0 % 0.96 65+ 55,848 16.8 % 25,214 30,634 45.1 % 54.9 % 0.82\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0254-625ff1f99c77:d03\", \"text\": \"Achada Furna is a settlement in the southern part of the island of Fogo, Cape Verde. It is situated 15 km east of the island capital São Filipe. At the 2010 census its population was 1,234. Its elevation is about 870 meters. Nearby places include Cabeça Fundão to the north, Figueira Pavão to the east, Fonte Aleixo to the south and Monte Largo to the west. Its climate is cooler than the low-lying areas of the island. The average temperature is. Average rainfall is 366 millimeters, the highest is 149 mm in September and the lowest is.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0254-625ff1f99c77:d04\", \"text\": \"3,564 1.1 % 1,822 1,743 51.1 % 48.9 % 1.05 < 5 18,827 5.7 % 9,624 9,203 51.1 % 48.9 % 1.05 < 15 60,467 18.2 % 30,989 29,578 51.2 % 48.8 % 1.05 15-24 43,089 13.0 % 21,996 21,092 51.0 % 49.0 % 1.04 25-34 45,495 13.7 % 23,053 22,442 50.7 % 49.3 % 1.03 35-44 43,40\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0254-625ff1f99c77:d05\", \"text\": \"Furna (Brava) Furna is a seaside community in the northeastern part of the island of Brava, Cape Verde. It lies 2.5 km northeast of the island capital of Nova Sintra. At the 2010 census its population was 612. The settlement was mentioned as \\\"Fuurno\\\" in the 1747 map by Jacques-Nicolas Bellin. Furna became the most important harbour of Brava in 1843. In 1982, many boats and some houses of Furna were destroyed by waves reaching a height of up to 10 meters which were caused by the tropical storm \\\"Beryl\\\". The harbour was improved in 2000. There are ferry connections\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0254-625ff1f99c77:d06\", \"text\": \"1,927,788 1,405,491 15.0 8.7 6.3 4.2 1.760 1979 224,567,000 3,494,398 1,913,841 1,580,557 15.6 8.5 7.1 3.9 1.808 1980 227,225,000 3,612,258 1,989,841 1,622,417 15.9 8.8 7.1 4.6 1.839 1981 229,466,000 3,629,238 1,977,981 1,651,257 15.8 8.6 7.2 2.6 1.812 1982 231,664,000 3,680,537 1,974,797 1,705,740 15.9 8.5 7.4 2.1 1.827 1983 233,792,000 3,638,933 2,019,201 1,619,732 15.6 8.6 6.9 2.2 1.799 1984 235,825,000 3,669,141 2,039,369 1,629,772 15.6 8.6 6.9 1.7 1.806 1985 237,924,000 3,760,561 2,086,440 1,674,121 15.8 8.8 7.0 1.8 1.844 1986 240,133,000 3,756,547 2,105,361 1,651,186 15.6 8.8 6.9 2.3 1.837 1987 242,289,000 3,809,394 2,123,323 1,686,071 15.7 8.8 7.0 1.9 1.872 1988 244,499,000 3,909,510\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ram